<title>USA: Zynaxis to be delisted from Nasdaq.</title>
<headline>Zynaxis to be delisted from Nasdaq.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zynaxis Inc said on Thursday its securities would be delisted from the Nasdaq SmallCap Market effective on December 24.</p>
<p>Zynaxis said its common stock would be considered a &quot;penny stock&quot; security, as defined under U.S. Securities law, and would trade in the &quot;over-the-counter&quot; market.</p>
<p>The company has agreed to merge with Vaxcel Inc, a unit of CytRx Corp to create a new public company. After closing, Vaxcel shares were expected to trade on the NASDAQ SmallCap market, Zynaxis said.</p>
</text>
